#. Tag: author
#: font-installation.docbook:5
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<personname> <firstname>Simon</firstname> <surname>Vermeersch</surname> </"
"personname> <email>titeuf@ph34rus.org</email>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: font-installation.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid "Fonts - Installing and Configuring"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: font-installation.docbook:17 font-installation.docbook:36
#: font-installation.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid "Fonts"
msgstr "Poliças"

#. Tag: para
#: font-installation.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Fonts are really easy to configure in &kde;. Open up the Control Center "
"(with <menuchoice><guimenu>K-Menu</guimenu><guimenuitem>Control Center</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>) and choose <guilabel>Font Installer</guilabel> in "
"<guilabel>System Administration</guilabel>in the tree view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: font-installation.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are two kinds of fonts: Personal and Global fonts. Personal fonts are "
"only accessible to your user, whereas global fonts are accessible to "
"everyone. When you open the <application>Font Installer</application>, "
"you're in Personal mode (you can see this in the <guilabel>Location</"
"guilabel> bar). When you click on the <guibutton>Administrator Mode</"
"guibutton> button, and put the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</"
"systemitem> password, you can access global mode, where you can change the "
"fonts for every user on this computer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: font-installation.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid "For the rest, there is no difference between those two kind of fonts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: font-installation.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid "previewing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: font-installation.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is a list of fonts in the center. Click on a font to see a preview. In "
"the toolbar on the top you have buttons to access the top directory, refresh "
"and change the view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: font-installation.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to, you can organise your fonts in multiple directories, so that "
"you can easily find them later."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: font-installation.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid "installing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: font-installation.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To install a font, click on the <guibutton>Add Fonts...</guibutton> button. "
"A file open dialog will appear where you can choose your font."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: font-installation.docbook:51
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can drag fonts from &konqueror; to the list. To remove a "
"font, <mousebutton>right</mousebutton> click on it and choose "
"<guibutton>Delete</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: font-installation.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuration (anti-aliasing)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: font-installation.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"kfontinst and kfontview should probably get a mention too, since they don't "
"seem to have any existing docs."
msgstr ""
